{"item_id": "77d2e211335e", "section": "Django 4.2 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.2 / Database backend API", "text": "inspectdb now uses display_size from DatabaseIntrospection.get_table_description() rather than internal_size for CharField."}
{"item_id": "9e90c3f96d8e", "section": "Django 4.2 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.2 / Dropped support for MariaDB 10.3", "text": "Upstream support for MariaDB 10.3 ends in May 2023. Django 4.2 supports MariaDB 10.4 and higher."}
{"item_id": "855ce00ef424", "section": "Django 4.2 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.2 / Dropped support for MySQL 5.7", "text": "Upstream support for MySQL 5.7 ends in October 2023. Django 4.2 supports MySQL 8 and higher."}
{"item_id": "28ca5aec2605", "section": "Django 4.2 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.2 / Dropped support for PostgreSQL 11", "text": "Upstream support for PostgreSQL 11 ends in November 2023. Django 4.2 supports PostgreSQL 12 and higher."}
{"item_id": "c2185fbe6ace", "section": "Django 4.2 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.2 / Setting update_fields in Model.save() may now be required", "text": "In order to avoid updating unnecessary columns, QuerySet.update_or_create now passes update_fields to the Model.save() calls. As a consequence, any fields modified in the custom save() methods should be added to the update_fields keyword argument before calling super(). See overriding-model-methods for more details."}
{"item_id": "2e973547a6eb", "section": "Django 4.2 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.2 / Dropped support for raw aggregations on MySQL", "text": "MySQL 8+ allows functional dependencies on GROUP BY columns, so the pre-Django 4.2 workaround of grouping by primary keys of the main table is removed. As a consequence, using RawSQL() aggregations is no longer supported on MySQL as there is no way to determine if such aggregations are needed or valid in the GROUP BY clause. Use aggregation-functions instead."}
{"item_id": "ff96fdf5226e", "section": "Django 4.2 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.2 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The undocumented django.http.multipartparser.parse_header() function is removed. Use django.utils.http.parse_header_parameters() instead."}
